        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): web_fetch leaves body open after provider fallback",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where `web_fetch` could leave an upstream response body open when a non-OK (or extraction-failed) response was abandoned after a successful provider fallback return. `finally` only called `release()`; the unread body was never cancelled.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nBefore returning a provider-fallback payload that abandons the direct fetch response, cancel the response body best-effort (`body?.cancel().catch(...)`), matching the cancel-before-release campaign used elsewhere in core.\n\n## User Impact\n\n**Before:** Successful provider fallback after a non-OK upstream could retain an unread response stream until GC.\n\n**After:** The abandoned upstream body is cancelled before returning the fallback payload; dispatcher release still runs in `finally`.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Proof (exit 0)\n\n```bash\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/tools/web-fetch.provider-fallback.test.ts -t \"cancels an unread non-OK\" --reporter=verbose\n```\n\n```text\n[web-fetch non-ok fallback cancel proof] cancelled=true extractor=custom-provider\n\n ✓ ... > cancels an unread non-OK response body when provider fallback succeeds\n Test Files  2 passed (2)\n      Tests  2 passed | 10 skipped (12)\n```\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n- **Behavior or issue addressed:** Non-OK upstream body is cancelled when provider fallback succeeds and returns early.\n- **Canonical reachability path:** `createWebFetchTool` → fetch non-OK → `maybeFetchProviderWebFetchPayload` success → `cancelUnreadWebFetchBody(res)` → return payload → `release()`.\n- **Boundary crossed:** Upstream HTTP error body stream → cancelled before fallback return.\n- **Shared helper / provider constraint check:** Local `cancelUnreadWebFetchBody` uses `body?.cancel().catch(() => undefined)` (same best-effort pattern as other cancel-unread helpers).\n- **Observed result after fix:** `cancelled=true extractor=custom-provider` (see proof log).\n- **Fix classification:** Root cause fix\n\n- [x] AI-assisted (Cursor)\n- [x] I understand what the code does\n- [x] Change is focused and does not mix unrelated concerns\n",
